# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/s6 window (the ship-6 candidate; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/s6 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt and
# ORDER-SHIP.txt have the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules of the two runs.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s6-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-s6-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory; the keys are the same in every
# smoke job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone. The replay and build steps do not forward the selection (the job reader refuses the keys beside them): they run the base checkpoint.
# A1 (EXACTNESS of the whole candidate, STOP): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s6-audit, the audited twin of the ship-6 candidate: every audit of the
# shipped ship-5 stack (the K/V page writer, the verify T2 audit, the pre-stage audits, the multi-user SDPA launch, the vglue, conv-gates and octo-lever audits, the 13x10
# grids, the host tier with every instrument on, the carry's audit, the hand-off's audit) and W3 WC with its audit (it rode the ship-5 twin in two card runs, 0 mismatches
# over ~12,800 audited rounds) PLUS the adaptive governor, on Swift. Tests: warmup; coding (one user, 1,500 tokens); np1_live2 and np1_live4 (two and four live seats: the
# counts WC acts at); prefill_few_decoders (the governor's own shape, audited); concurrent8_drain (eight users whose budgets end one by one: every live count from 8 to 1);
# concurrent8_steady (the octo rounds, required by the smoke check on this profile); agent_turns last. READ: c2_smoke_check clean (its fusion, octo, grid13, WC and governor
# rules read the container log); every audit line exact=True with entries above 0; octo_judge.py --container-log <container log> --profile
# c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s6-audit clean; NO "audit mismatch", NO "fell back" but the octo block's one WC line, NO "kv shared", no stall. W3 WC:
# the "[PINDIAG] tp4 gdn wc engaged" line (conv_cores, gate_cores and z_cores above 0) once per engine start that has an M3 block, a "gdn wc audit <n> exact=True" line on
# the audited twin and no "audit mismatch"; the octo block (8 users of 8 rows) declines it with ONE "[PINDIAG] tp4 gdn wc fell back reason=8 users (WC takes 2 or 4)" line,
# which is the design (w3_wc_smoke accepts exactly that line); any other "fell back" line fails. GOVERNOR: the install line "[PINDIAG] lever N adaptive: decoders<=2
# share=0.9 ttft=120 gap_floor=8" once; every scheduler step line carries base=, target= and adaptive=; adaptive=1 exactly on the prefill steps that ran with one or two
# decoders live (and the base share 0.9, the target 120); adaptive=0 and today's 0.5/180 with none or three or more; f_eff never below base
# (c2_smoke_check.levern_adaptive_problems judges all of it; prefill_few_decoders NOT EXERCISED means no step was adaptive). The decode-gap floor (8 s) holds: no gap over
# it in the decoders of prefill_few_decoders. Then python3 scripts/ci/sched_report.py <container log>. The audited profile holds about 2.6 GB more DRAM per chip than the
# unaudited one (the ship-5 window: A1 timed out three agent-turn reads on admission holds that T1B did not have): a hold line on this job is the audit's own weight, not
# the candidate's, and it is not a stop reason by itself. ANY audit mismatch, a WC or governor refusal, or a stall is NO-GO for the candidate and halts the window.
# agent_turns (6 sessions of 64k, 128k and 200k tokens, 12 returning turns each) is the MAIN JUDGE: the ship-5 window's T1B number (50.36 tok/s aggregate, returning turn
# first token p50 1.46 s, p90 2.33 s) is its baseline. agent_turns8 is EIGHT sessions weighted like production traffic (contexts of 24k to 80k tokens and one of ~200k,
# about 550k tokens in all, mean ~69k against production's ~59k; answers capped at 300 to 1,080 tokens, mean 690 like production's; the same gaps and 12 turns), every seat
# busy, no new turn after 25 minutes, an estimate of 15 minutes: the production load, where WC (2 or 4 users) and the governor (1 or 2 decoders) mostly sit out, so the pair
# says whether anything is LOST there. Compare it with its own control leg, never with agent_turns. Read both legs with `python3 scripts/ci/agent_turns.py report
# --smoke-log <smoke> --container-log <container> --test <name>`: the rates, the TTFT by context bucket, the tokens re-prefilled, the per-live table; the per-turn answer
# hashes must be EQUAL between the legs. CHECKPOINT READ (the workflow passes c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint): the container log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint
# ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4 key=... weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is not read or written)"
# once, a "weight cache ...: found" line (the cache the Swift window built; this pack never builds it) and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint bound ..." line; the models
# answer names ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b. TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1, scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a second through
# the smoke step; the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. A rate difference that comes with a different loaded AICLK between the arms is the clocks, not the
# lever. RUN WITH THE CI PAUSED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job beside it. Duration (estimate): 115
# minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s6-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s6-audit
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,np1_live2,np1_live4,prefill_few_decoders,concurrent8_drain,concurrent8_steady,agent_turns
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=190
